// The internal inline function h is inlined into main (a friend module); the inlined body
// constructs the private class C, whose primary constructor has a default value. In main's
// per-file cache the construction is lowered to the synthetic $default constructor stub
// C#<init>(Int, Int, DefaultConstructorMarker?) and referenced as an external symbol, but
// lib1's per-file cache emits that stub with LLVM internal linkage: ContextUtils.linkageOf
// propagates isCalledFromExportedInlineFunction through irFunction.originalConstructor, while
// the stub only carries the common attribute defaultArgumentsOriginalFunction
// (DefaultArgumentFunctionFactory) and falls back to itself, where the flag is not set
// (CacheInfoBuilder.trackCallees sets it only on the real constructor). The link fails with
// an undefined symbol while the same klibs link and print 1 without incremental compilation.
//
// Harness note: the "clean" reference link also enables incremental compilation (with a fresh
// cache), so this from-scratch IC-only defect fails both of the harness's links and the run
// is reported as INVALID. The bug is the IC-only link failure: the same klibs link and print
// 1 without -Xenable-incremental-compilation.

MODULES: lib1, main

STEP 0:
    libs: lib1, main
